# Remote compilation helper artifacts
.rch-target/
# Per-job target shards created by `rch` when multiple cargo invocations
# run concurrently (suffix is target-set + job-id + nanos + retry counter).
.rch-target-*/
# The shared pool is plural with no separator, so neither pattern above matches
# it. It is a symlink into /data/tmp/rch-targets-pool.
.rch-targets/
.rch-deploy-root/
rch-bin/
rch-install/

# Agent mail project identity
.agent-mail-project-id
target-codex*/
target_*/
target-local/

# Local legacy-oracle mirrors (too large for source repo)
/legacy_*/

# Ephemeral files (agent-generated, build artifacts, test detritus)
ci-artifacts/
test_meminfo

# proptest-regressions/ is deliberately NOT ignored (frankentorch-wly7k). It was filed under
# "test detritus" above, which is backwards: those files are the durable record of every
# counterexample proptest has ever found, and proptest re-runs them BEFORE generating novel
# cases. The file's own generated header says "It is recommended to check this file in to
# source control so that everyone who runs the test benefits from these saved cases."
# Ignoring it meant eleven accumulated seeds were replayed for one checkout and invisible to
# every other agent and to a fresh clone — which is precisely how a lucky-seed discovery fails
# to become a permanent regression case (see frankentorch-jabbh).

